Oliviu Craznic
Pivnitele Palatului Charron (Beneath The Charron Palace)
Un preot este rapit in toiul noptii de doi barbati misteriosi si fortat sa ingrijeasca ranile unei tinere legate in lanturi. Intre timp, doi nobili urmaresc un capitan englez, vinovat de viol si abuzuri. Un Dumnezeu nemilos si absent le poarta tuturor destinele catre finalul tragic, in pivnitele unui adept al demonolatrului Conrad Lorenz. Dar poate ca absenta divinului din acel loc cumplit nu este tocmai ceea ce pare, iar interventia cereasca isi are forme si motivatii revelate doar inocentilor...
Detinator a numeroase premii, dintre care unul european, Oliviu Craznic, autorul romanului de succes ...Si la sfarsit a mai ramas cosmarul (un ,,gothic romance" de epoca, o poveste cu vampiri medievali) si al seriei ,,military space opera" Ermengaarde Saga (povestea unei frumoase si controversate principese, intr-un univers sfasiat de razboi, tradare, pasiune si ura), ne prezinta aici o scurta, dar intensa povestire din lumea Cosmarului, povestire in care cititorii vor regasi incantati, asa cum au solicitat in repetate randuri, personajele indragite ale romanului favorit.
Ciprian Mitoceanu
In padure (Through The Woods)
Obligat de parinti sa participe impreuna cu ei la excursia familiala traditionala, un adolescent descopera terifiat ca a nu ajunge la petrecerea organizata de fata iubita nu este nici pe departe cel mai rau lucru de pe Pamant. Adevaruri zac ingropate in codru ca si in inimile noastre, iar sacrificiile pe care le fac cei dragi pentru tine pot schimba lumi, lasand in urma doar o marturie si oase...
Profesor de istorie si creator al apreciatei serii science-fiction Amendamentul Dawson, dar si autor al romanului thriller Coltii, Ciprian Mitoceanu ne ofera, in acest numar special dedicat sufletelor pierdute si locatiilor bantuite, o nuveleta plina de intrebari, invataminte si... spaime.
DUBLU TAIS
De citit vineri noaptea."∂
≥O planeta se stinge, indepartandu-se de stelele vecine si indreptandu-se spre teritoriul frigului, al intunericului si al mortii. Odata cu ea, vor pieri paisprezece orase. Iar eroul, parasit de iubita, nu mai gaseste sensul vietii.
Un space-opera de neuitat, romanul de debut al lui George R.R. Martin infatiseaza o viziune provocatoare asupra noptii eterne. In Lumina ce se stinge palpita o lume in care coabiteaza mai multe culturi, unde prada si vanatorul isi schimba adesea rolurile.
George R.R. Martin a scris un roman al disparitiei si al temerilor. Lumina ce se stinge dezvaluie o scriitura rafinata, pusa la lucru intr-o fictiune ce-si rasplateste cu asupra de masura cititorul.
,,Lumina ce se stinge mi-a spulberat iluziile despre ce este si ce poate face fictiunea, despre puterea imaginatiei."
Michael Chabon"–	
Õ	Moving. Disturbing. In Denver, a young woman grows up terrorized by something massive and unnatural that watches her while she sleeps. In west Texas, a boy's world unravels as his brother relates an encounter with a strange figure in the woods. Struggling with insomnia and depression, a man named Mitch begins speaking to a creature of folklore in the trees behind his house. And along the plains of the Rocky Mountains, two college students discover a house that should not exist.
These stories and more make up Karl Pfeiffer's first collection following his debut novel, Hallowtide. Ranging from fiction to non-fiction, from the poetic to the profane, Into a Sky Below, Forever examines the thin places, where the wild leaks into the refined, the supernatural bleeds into the physical, reality blends with fiction, and where the only things left holding the world together are the things that truly matter the most.
This is a book about birth and rebirth: it's a study of cycles, sex, and ouroboric processes; it's an examination of the ways we grow up, grow strong, grow together, and grow apart; an autopsy of the ways we love and rage and reproduce and repeat again.
As always, it's about finding light amidst the darkness."ﬂ
‹In this beloved novel, #1 New York Timesbestselling author Sherryl Woods proves once again that sometimes family does know best.
Straitlaced tycoon Richard Carlton suspects that his Aunt Destiny has more than business matters on her mind when she insists he meet klutzy PR executive Melanie Hart. Melanie might be brilliant-and beautiful-but Richard won't open his wounded heart to any woman, no matter how much she might make his pulse race.
Yet when the press mistakenly reports that they're a couple, Richard convinces Melanie to pretend that they're engaged-to bolster his reputation and to teach his matchmaking aunt a lesson, once and for all. But is this relationship just a charade, or do opposites really attract-for keeps?"‚
